            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Our EE informed us that the presence pins of the VT, AALC, and rack leak sensors need to be logged as event logs. However, these pins are already used by the gpio-presence-sensor in the gpiopresence service. Is there any way to log presence/not present status as event logs in this case?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "The clients need to rely on the hardware inventory for inventory presence. There are no events for inventory at the moment. Please inform them accordingly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "I see."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Opening this chat again. Since, these are the cables, they can be added to the cable monitor config to raise the events if the cable gets disconnected. I had already mentioned to Yang Chen (you are cced too) to do the Cable monitor testing earlier via email. Sent u the email again. So, lets do that. Also lets add a default cable monitor config into the ventura openbmc layer, so its always staged. (FYI: On Meta Internal side we have an off the box service which stages this cable monitor config)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "We've added cable-config.json into the Ventura OpenBMC layer. Please help review the following PRs. Thanks!\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/openbmc/+/82770\nhttps://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/82752"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged, Will review those PRs. Thanks"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/ventura_scm.json",
                    "line": 259,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Are these actual leak sensors or the cable presence pins?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/ventura_scm.json",
                    "line": 259,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "P. K. Lee",
                        "email": "p.k.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "PKLee-Quanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Oh, I missed the word 'Port'. These are cable presence pins. Thanks for the reminder!"
                }
